## Tracker

- active: {{TRACKER_ACTIVE}}       <!-- github | local -->
- local-path: `.scratch/`
- language: {{LANGUAGE}}           <!-- en | cs -->

`/analyze` writes the analysis prose in this language — title and every section body. Section headings stay English, as do identifiers, paths and HTTP contracts. `/implement` and `/verify` comments on the **analysis** (never on the PR) use the same language. `/verify` green (agent): ready PR + `ready-to-review`. `/verify` fail (agent): draft PR, `needs-attention` (replaces `in-progress`), fail note on the analysis.

When `active: local`, see `docs/agents/issue-tracker.local.md` (if present) for file conventions.

## UX review

- ux-review: {{UX_REVIEW}}   <!-- enabled | disabled -->

**enabled** — `/verify` Phase 3, after code review is green; hard gate on Critical/Major; after UX fixes re-run local tooling before Ship.

**disabled** — Ship right after code review is green.

Code review itself (Phase 2) has no switch — it always runs.

## Skills

- skills-dir: {{SKILLS_DIR}}   <!-- .cursor/skills | .claude/skills | .agents/skills -->

Vendored by `/setup`; re-running `/setup` overwrites them. Repo-specific additions go to `docs/agents/`, never into the vendored files.

## Work types

| Type | Pipeline | branch-owner typical |
|------|----------|----------------------|
| **feature** | `/align` → `/analyze` → `/implement` → `/verify` (functional → code review [→ ux] → ship) | agent (full-agentic) or human (human-owned) |
| **complex bug** | same as feature; `/align` if root cause unclear | agent or human |
| **simple bug** | skip `/align`; ticket with Acceptance → `/implement` | human |
| **trivial fix** | outside pipeline — direct fix + commit | n/a |

### Bug fast-path

1. Create bug issue (GitHub with `analysis` omitted, or `.scratch/analysis/NNN-slug.md` with `Kind: bug`; next ID shared with `.scratch/analysis/done/`) with Acceptance.
2. `/implement #issue` implements Acceptance from the ticket body, then runs `/verify`. User-invoked `/implement` does not need `ready-for-agent`.

## Session override

User may pass `/implement #N human` or `/implement #N agent` to override branch-owner for one session.
